        "result": "RETRIED PER COORDINATOR INSTRUCTION on a fresh network state: the trimmed 10-file prefetch (tokenizer + config + pytorch_model.bin, excluding optimizer.pt/scheduler.pt/rng_state.pth/model.safetensors) completed cleanly in 2m36s, confirming the network was fine and the earlier stalls were transient/environmental, not file-specific. However GLiNER.from_pretrained(..., local_files_only=True) then refused to load: huggingface_hub.errors.IncompleteSnapshotError, because it validates the cached snapshot against the repo's FULL original file manifest (all 14 files) rather than only the files it actually reads for inference -- it considers the deliberately-skipped optimizer.pt/model.safetensors \"missing\" even though nothing in the inference path touches them. Without local_files_only, from_pretrained triggers its OWN internal snapshot_download of the full (untrimmed) repo regardless of what was already prefetched, re-attempting exactly the multi-GB transfer that stalled in attempts 1-3."
